module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_parameter_default_value_is_never_judged_against_its_parameter_type

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BelowCeiling, FoundBelowTheLadder, RecurringFailureMode, RungRead }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { StructurallyGuaranteed }
import gunbc.rung_climb { ClimbableButUnbuilt }

data a_parameter_default_value_is_never_judged_against_its_parameter_type: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_parameter_default_value_is_never_judged_against_its_parameter_type" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungRead { found_at: FoundBelowTheLadder, standing: BelowCeiling { current: FoundBelowTheLadder, ceiling: StructurallyGuaranteed, blocker: ClimbableButUnbuilt, trigger_capability: "every declared parameter default is inferred at its declared type and judged by the declared-type relation at PositionParameterDefault, refusing a default that does not inhabit it" } },

  receipts: [
    "**a parameter default value is never inferred or judged on the gunbc compile path** (`fn f(v: Nat = \"x\") -> Nat { v }` is accepted: the default is a value of the wrong kind and nothing refuses or warns, so every call that omits the argument receives it).",

    "INVALID STATE, stronger than 'not judged against its type': a parameter default's EXPRESSION is never inferred on the compile path, so a default that does not inhabit its parameter's declared type, or that is itself ill-formed, is accepted with no diagnostic that differs from a correct default. `h(v: Wrap = Wrap { n: \"x\" })` is the decisive specimen: a record literal with a wrong field is refused everywhere it IS inferred, so its silence is a reach defect (the default is not visited), not an answer of the declared-type relation.",

    "RECEIPT (2026-10-31, sunny-newt-661, srv1, systemd scope RuntimeMaxSec=1800 MemoryMax=16G MemorySwapMax=0). Command: `cd ~/sn-own/src && ~/sn-own/gunbc compile --source-root ~/sn-own/src/sn_fx --source-root ~/sn-own/src/dag --entry ~/sn-own/src/sn_fx/dp/p.dag --output-dir ~/sn-own/out`, entry `module dp.p` with `type Wrap = Wrap { n: Int }`, `fn f(v: Wrap = 3) -> Int { 0 }`, `fn g(v: Nat = \"x\") -> Nat { v }`, `fn h(v: Wrap = Wrap { n: \"x\" }) -> Int { 0 }`. Revision: the clone ~/sn-own/src HEAD ca41cf39e192e261784e622afd85e199d7a9882b (kh/q1-q2-validation). Binary sha256 f46dc37cd1130c33e5776aca46f6fd2cf15bd92b5567dd256f06e6c3b7341024. Scope: one compile of one entry, frontend stages only; every frontend stage (compile.frontend, normalize, reconcile, analyses) completed and printed ZERO diagnostics for f, g and h; the process then exited 3 at the emit stage (`WorkspaceNotRealized: EmitterReverseEdge std_algebra -> dp_p`), which is unrelated to the question. sha256 of the filtered output (the `[pre-entry]` timing lines removed): 025fbca4445d44e4d8669ba6a8fb76d3f46394ee3493a26d51ccdda8b1fd9bcc. Not established: that the same holds on another binary or entry.",

    "REACH CAUSE: UNDER TRACE, not asserted. Read so far on the compile path: the parser keeps a default as the param node's second child (parse_param, make_param_node), resolve_param keeps the resolved default (make_resolved_param_node), analyze_item stores the resolved params on the item, and infer_item's fn branches call parameter_default_emissions over item.params. None of these drops it by reading, so where the default stops being visited is not yet located; the trace is not complete and no cause is claimed.",

    "SPECIMEN, found 2026-10-31 by execution (sunny-newt-661, route 5 of the Q1b E1b literal-route census). Command: `gunbc run --source-root dag --entry <probe> --function <fn>` over a probe module that builds `module dp.p ... fn f(v: Nat = <default>) -> Nat { v }` and reads `compile_dag_diagnostic_census` (census_total_count, census_blocking_rows, CensusNotRunnable). Revision: kh/q1d-builtin-parameter-obligation e0dfd7aeb6d, binary sha256 prefix f6c9e59c3d84 (built from tree dd798283). Defaults tried: `3` (control), `\"x\"`, `0 - 5`, `Wrap { n: 1 }`. Output sums, identical across all four: blocking-rows-zero true, total-rows-zero false (the same non-blocking baseline rows as the control), not-runnable false. 4 defaults x 3 cells = 12 cells; the three wrong-kind defaults are indistinguishable from the control.",

    "WHY IT SURVIVES: argument positions are judged by direct_call_argument_inhabitance_diags (and, since Q1d, builtin arguments); the default expression is never routed through it, so it is a fourth unjudged route beside the literal-introduction routes. E1b and E1 do not reach it: they act where an expected type is supplied, and a default is never given one.",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: supply the parameter's declared type as `expected` to the default expression and run the argument obligation on it. RED: the four defaults above; positive control: `3`.",

    "SECOND TRIGGER, stated so it is not a silent gap: the repair on q1-param-default-obligation keeps only the default's DIAGNOSTICS; the typed default is not stored back on the param node and emission still reads the untyped default, so a literal introduced at its carrier (Q1b E1b) does not yet reach an emitted default. Visibility is module scope only: stage0 call_function_inner evaluates a default in the caller-supplied env, and v1.compiler.emit_rust fill_default_args / fill_op_default_args splice it at the call site; neither binds a sibling parameter.",

    "SIBLING FINDING (Q1b step 2, not this row's fix): String at std.nat Nat reaches declared_type_inhabitance's terminal UnmodeledNoArmDecides, wrong code the RELATION itself should refuse; the kernel-at-structured arm exempts grounded carriers by design. Hypothesis from reading, to be confirmed by the pre-fix probe. The relation fix belongs to Q1b, not to the default position.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
